From 6162e8b14119c9763ee28e743d2d47841815f6b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:36:51 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(circular): judge a whole-model Circular against the
 finished part

A Circular whose source is the finished part (SrcRef::Entity, part_solid)
took DepthLaw::None, so a circle typed through the part's wall generated
with no warning on the operation; only the program-level stock sim held
the post. It now takes DepthLaw::Section through one shared law,
authored_law(src), written for the kinds that cut geometry typed by hand
(Circular now, the Slot of #1537 next): an Entity source is judged, a
Stock source still cuts unjudged, a picked Circular keeps its law.

Pinned by circular_entity_law.rs (wall convicted and the post blocked,
legal circle clean and path unchanged, Stock unjudged, MCP parity) and
operation::authored_law_tests (the law table).

Fixes #1543

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL
